hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17385","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Bishr, he said haddathana Muhammad ibn Amr, he said haddathana Abu Kathir, freedman of the Laythiyyin, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Jahsh, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is for me if I am killed in the path of Allah. He said: Paradise. When he turned, he said: Except debt, Jibril (peace be upon him) told it to me just now."
"17386","Haddathana Khalaf ibn al-Walid, haddathana Abbad ibn Abbad, haddathana Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abi Kathir, freedman of the Hilaliyyin, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Jahsh, from his father, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is for me if I fight in the path of Allah until I am killed. He said: Paradise. He said: When he turned, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Except debt, Jibril (peace be upon him) told it to me just now."
